From f73ca25b747f93d760368c58a70abdf89024a54c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duckfamily <156525766+duckfamily@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 02:33:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] Add the Sealgram settings section

Security, Privacy, Network, Appearance and Updates, plus a connection
dashboard under Network showing live state: the current proxy and its
response time, whether media is flowing, every known proxy sorted by
measured ping with its badges, and a history of automatic switches with the
reason for each.

The dashboard answers the question the log could answer and the interface
could not: why did it switch, and why is it slow. Rows are clickable to
switch by hand; the measure button deliberately does not switch.

Security is informational only. There are no controls there that weaken the
hardening or reset the TPM key, because a control that quietly destroys
every sealed profile is not a setting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
